ves the sorry-free transport from absolute Grassmannian H-quasi-projectivity to the chosen field representer using global freeness, base change, and representer uniqueness.\n- [DemandLedger.lean](/home/axel/LeanAlgebraicGeometry-Horizon/MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge/AlgebraicJacobian/Projective/DemandLedger.lean:157) now isolates the valid-rank absolute `toSpecZ` certificate as the remaining D4 producer.\n- Cleanup commit `5bed069cc6e6` changed only `DemandLedger.lean`, removing disconnected section-Proj placeholders. Classification remains cleanup-only: producer `+0`, seam `+0`.\n- Metadata is durable in `8c88b6283b`, roadmap state in `3291c13956`, and boundary notice `I-1832` in `1ec5eed60c`.\n\nFinal narrow build passed for both projective modules. All eight public declarations were axiom-audited: proved declarations use only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`; the two intentional producers retain `sorryAx`. No `(rep :)` consumer binder was added.\n\n## Issues\n\n- The valid-rank absolute Grassmannian Pl\u00fccker/projective-space certificate remains open.\n- D3 still lacks an actual base-locus scheme, map to the Grassmannian, and quasi-compact immersion. The generic D4 wrapper is only a typecheck.\n- Relative Proj and ampleness remain pending because no concrete Picard component consumes them. Very-ampleness continues to reuse `IsHQuasiProjectiveWith`.\n- Full hgraph sync found 142 pre-existing stale nodes and 28 duplicate declarations; only six owned nodes were committed.\n\n## Why I stopped\n\nFurther progress requires either constructing the Pl\u00fccker embedding or receiving the real D3 locus map. Building general relative-Proj or ampleness theory now would violate the demand gate. Producer movement and seam movement therefore remain `+0`.\n\nThe expensive umbrella build was not run; both affected modules were built directly.\n\n## Next\n\n1. Construct the valid-rank Pl\u00fccker immersion and prove `Grassmannian.toSpecZ` H-quasi-projective.\n2. Build the actual D3 Grassmannian-base locus and quasi-compact immersion.\n3. Consume the existing conditional transport theorem, then reconsider Proj or ampleness only if the represented Picard component exposes a concrete signature.", "tool": "", "data": {}, "usage": null, "_cursor": 3773714}, {"kind": "text", "at": "2026-08-03T04:49:59.356872+00:00", "text": "The only mutating action after the final ledger commit was the cached `lake build`, which writes ignored build artifacts. I\u2019m rechecking every authored source and state blob against current `HEAD` so the checkpoint can close without an empty commit.", "tool": "", "data": {}, "usage": null, "_cursor": 3776263}, {"kind": "tool_call", "at": "2026-08-03T04:50:16.969469+00:00", "text": "", "tool": "Bash", "data": {"command": "/bin/bash -lc '\"$HORIZON_GIT\" rev-parse \"HEAD:MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge/AlgebraicJacobian/Projective/Grassmannian.lean\"'"}, "usage": null, "_cursor": 3776624}, {"kind": "tool_result", "at": "2026-08-03T04:50:16.969482+00:00", "text": "", "tool": "Bash", "data": {"content": "a22b515331a2aca21adff73dd2c6e557941a1826\n", "exit_code": 0}, "usage": null, "_cursor": 3776896}, {"kind": "tool_call", "at": "2026-08-03T04:50:16.977772+00:00", "text": "", "tool": "Bash", "data": {"command": "/bin/bash -lc '\"$HORIZON_GIT\" hash-object \"MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge/AlgebraicJacobian/Projective/Grassmannian.lean\"'"}, "usage": null, "_cursor": 3777088}, {"kind": "tool_result", "at": "2026-08-03T04:50:16.977784+00:00", "text": "", "tool": "Bash", "data": {"content": "a22b515331a2aca21adff73dd2c6e557941a1826\n", "exit_code": 0}, "usage": null, "_cursor": 3777357}, {"kind": "tool_call", "at": "2026-08-03T04:50:16.978949+00:00", "text": "", "tool": "Bash", "data": {"command": "/bin/bash -lc '\"$HORIZON_GIT\" rev-parse \"HEAD:MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge/AlgebraicJacobian/Projective/DemandLedger.lean\"'"}, "usage": null, "_cursor": 3777549}, {"k